hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"469","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When a riding animal is held as collateral, it may be ridden because of the expenditure on it, and a milking animal's milk may be drunk. Whoever rides or drinks the milk will bear the expense."
"470","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A mortgaged animal may be ridden in exchange for its maintenance, and a milking animal, when it is mortgaged, its milk may be drunk in exchange for its maintenance. And whoever rides or drinks its milk, its maintenance is his responsibility."
"471","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The mortgaged animal may be ridden and its milk may be drunk."
